Embedded React: scope the fade cache to its group, and keep it from thrashing.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/compositor.c and
engine/tests/rendering/test_opacity.c. Not yet proposed upstream.

The fade cache (ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W/H) blends one captured copy of a fading
group instead of re-rendering it every frame, but any content change anywhere
on screen dropped the copy: a focus ring's moving light or a progress bar
elsewhere made every frame a miss. Its copy holds only the group's subtree,
blended over whatever is under it, so only a change inside the group can make
it stale. The content generation now advances only for a change in the cached
group's subtree. A nested opacity value inside the group counts as such a
change: it was marked visual-only, and a cached group showed it frozen.

One slot serves every translucent group, so a small static one (a 60% ring)
and a fading screen evicted each other on alternate frames and neither hit. A
smaller group no longer takes the slot from a larger one composited in this
commit or the last; it takes the strip path, as without the cache.

Without ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W/H nothing changes.

--- a/engine/scene/compositor.c
+++ b/engine/scene/compositor.c
@@ -550,11 +550,46 @@
         s_cur_buf = (s_cur_buf + 1) % s_display_buffer_count;
 }
 
-/* Global content generation: advanced by every mutation that changes rendered subtree content
- * (er_mark_dirty_upward and friends). The fade cache stores the generation it captured at; any
- * bump invalidates it. Deliberately coarse — a content change anywhere invalidates the one
- * cached subtree — which keeps the check O(1) and always correct. */
+/* Content generation of the fade cache's subtree: advanced by every mutation that changes rendered
+ * content inside the cached group (er_mark_dirty_upward and friends walk up through it). The fade
+ * cache stores the generation it captured at; any bump invalidates it. A change outside the group
+ * leaves the copy valid: the copy holds only the group's own subtree, blended over whatever is under
+ * it. A visual-only mark (an opacity value) below the group changes its content too; only the
+ * group's own opacity does not. */
 static uint32_t s_content_gen = 1U;
+#if defined(ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W) && defined(ERUI_FADE_CACHE_H) && ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W > 0 && ERUI_FADE_CACHE_H > 0
+/* Defined with the fade cache below; 0xFFFF when nothing is cached. */
+static uint16_t s_fade_cache_tag;
+#endif
+
+/**
+ * @brief Advances the content generation when `node` lies in the cached group's subtree.
+ * @param[in] node   The changed node.
+ * @param[in] self   Whether the group's own change counts (false for its own opacity value).
+ */
+static void bump_content_gen_within(const ERNode* node, bool self)
+{
+#if !(defined(ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W) && defined(ERUI_FADE_CACHE_H) && ERUI_FADE_CACHE_W > 0 && ERUI_FADE_CACHE_H > 0)
+    (void)node;
+    (void)self;
+    s_content_gen++;
+    return;
+#else
+    /* A node in a display:none subtree paints nothing (see er_mark_dirty_upward_visual); showing it
+     * again changes the shown ancestor, which counts. */
+    if (s_fade_cache_tag == 0xFFFFu || !node || node->subtree_hidden)
+        return;
+    for (const ERNode* at = node; at; at = er_get_node(at->parent_tag))
+    {
+        if (at->tag == s_fade_cache_tag)
+        {
+            if (self || at != node)
+                s_content_gen++;
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+}
 
 /* Source of content_stamp values; starts above the 0 a fresh node holds. */
 static uint32_t s_content_stamp = 1U;
